328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (I first want to preface by saying I think quantum is mostly a LARP. From my view, we are very far away from being able to build a computer with enough qubits to do anything useful, we can't even get our current ones to run shor's algo without a million hacks. However I do think it'll happen one day, when we've built a dyson sphere and have cities on Mars, we probably will have figured it out by then. That day could be faster than I expect \(certainly was for AI\) but it seems this is more of a physical and engineering problem rather than a math / theory problem, which are much harder to solve.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
